Expected elements: present

All four changes are visible and three landed cleanly. The provenance note is now flush-left in a grid-spanning `dd` (Transaction pane, y204–386); `COST · TRANSACTIONFEE` reads `1755555891986239551` / `mana (FeeJuice)` on two lines at y553–582 instead of a wrapped hex word, and it no longer breaks the label/value grid; the exit reads `← aztec-testnet` and no demo-fixture content leaks in. No invented source anywhere — no file tab, listing, line number, function or variable name. Each affected pane explains itself in its own words, and `Supply sources` is present at y285–311.

Through the density lens the split is the story, and the queued observation is worse, not resolved. Measured: the Code pane is 912px wide with last ink at y309 — 78% of its 980px body empty; Call Trace is 574px tall holding 32px of ink, 91% empty; Values 86% empty. The Transaction pane is the narrowest column at 382px and the only one overflowing: its `RAW (CHAIN-NATIVE)` JSON is sliced mid-glyph by the pane border at y1075 on `"hydrationRounds": 6,` with no scrollbar or fade, and `effectsMismatched` — the expectation's evidence the replay was faithful — falls below that cut and appears nowhere else on the page.

The band's removal has not paid off at 1920: the DATA row costs 216px, 22% of the Transaction pane body, because a 42-character measure wraps the note to eight lines — and that cost now lands on the one starved pane.

Fixes: take width from the 912px Code pane; promote the replay counters to labelled rows above RAW.

Rating: 6/10

